  "description": "A high-performance object-to-object mapper for .NET. Mapping delegates are\n      compiled once per type pair via Expression Trees and cached for the lifetime\n      of the IMapper instance — no reflection, no boxing, on the hot path.\n      Supports bi-directional mapping, property flattening, unflattening, nullable\n      coercion, numeric widening, enum conversion, collection mapping with DFS\n      cycle detection, and EF Core-compatible ProjectTo SQL projection.\n      v3.0 added mapping into an existing instance, ConstructUsing for types without\n      a parameterless constructor, per-member Condition and NullSubstitute, BeforeMap\n      / AfterMap lifecycle hooks, configurable recursion depth (MaxDepth) for\n      self-referencing types, and AssertConfigurationIsValid startup validation.\n      v4.0 added collection merge into an existing collection, configurable\n      flatten/unflatten lookahead depth (FlattenDepth), reusable IValueResolver\n      classes for ForMember, polymorphic/inheritance mapping (Include), and\n      recursive AssertConfigurationIsValid into nested complex-type pairs.\n      v5.0 adds DI-resolved value resolvers (MapFrom<TResolver,TMember>()\n      via a Mapper constructed with an IServiceProvider), ForAllMembers blanket\n      per-pair member rules, and identity-based collection diffing\n      (EqualityComparison) for add/update/remove merges into an existing collection.\n      v5.1 extends Include-based polymorphic dispatch beyond top-level calls: elements\n      of a mapped collection and nested complex members now map on their runtime type\n      (a Dog inside a List<Animal>, or a nested Animal member holding a Dog, maps\n      to DogDto), paid only for pairs that declare Include<>.\n      v6.0 multi-targets net8.0 and net10.0 (LTS coverage back to .NET 8) and adds the\n      boilerplate-free Map<TDestination>(source) overload that infers the source\n      type from the object's runtime type — dispatch is resolved once, compiled, and\n      cached, and the explicit two-generic path is unchanged.\n      v7.0 maps nested collection properties (Order.Lines: List<OrderLine> to\n      List<OrderLineDto>) in both the runtime engine and ProjectTo (as a\n      SQL-translatable nested Select), constructs positional records and immutable\n      ctor-only types by matching constructor parameters to source properties with\n      zero configuration, adds global null-safe ConvertUsing type converters, lets\n      BeforeMap/AfterMap hooks accumulate, and adds DI-resolved IMappingAction\n      classes. Ships SourceLink, symbol packages, and deterministic CI builds.",
